# SURA integrity policy: byte-exact checkouts on every platform.
#
# Why: the Phase-7 integrity checkpoint (data/phase7_checkpoint.md) and tests such as
# tests/test_phase7b.py and tests/test_chunk_candidates.py pin SHA-256 hashes of file BYTES.
# With core.autocrlf=true (the common Git-for-Windows default), text files are checked out
# with CRLF endings, every pinned LF-blob hash mismatches, and those tests fail for
# environment reasons rather than product reasons.
#
# `* -text` disables ALL line-ending conversion by Git (checkout and commit) for tracked
# files, so the working tree always matches the stored blob bytes exactly - on Windows,
# Linux and macOS alike. Historical artifacts that were committed with CRLF bytes
# (e.g. some data/evaluation/phase12_* files from a Windows capture) keep their exact
# bytes too; nothing is renormalized, no pinned hash changes.
#
# Consequence: new text files must be committed with the endings their producer wrote.
# Tooling in this repository generates LF; keep it that way.
* -text
